 ["K",2,"Dividing buyers into groups by the different benefits they want from a product is:",["Benefit segmentation","Geographic segmentation","Demographic segmentation","Occasion segmentation"],"Benefit segmentation is a type of behavioural segmentation.","2026-10-21T19:12:00+05:00"],
 ["K",2,"Dividing buyers by when they get the idea to buy, when they buy or when they use a product is:",["Occasion segmentation","Benefit segmentation","Psychographic segmentation","Geographic segmentation"],"Eid, weddings and school holidays are buying occasions.","2026-10-21T19:12:00+05:00"],
 ["K",2,"An advantage over competitors gained by offering greater customer value, through lower prices or more benefits, is a:",["Competitive advantage","Value chain","Market segment","Brand extension"],"The advantage must be real and meaningful to target customers.","2026-10-21T19:12:00+05:00"],
 ["K",2,"A chart that shows how consumers see brands compared with each other on important buying dimensions is a:",["Perceptual positioning map","BCG growth-share matrix","SWOT analysis","Product/market expansion grid"],"Positioning maps show where each brand sits in buyers' minds.","2026-10-21T19:12:00+05:00"],
 ["K",3,"A positioning statement usually follows which form?",["To (target segment and need) our (brand) is (concept) that (point of difference)","Our brand is the cheapest in the market","We sell (product) at (price) in (place)","(Brand) is for everyone, everywhere"],"It names the target, the brand, the category and the difference.","2026-10-21T19:12:00+05:00"],
 ["K",3,"Tailoring products and marketing programmes to the needs and preferences of one customer at a time is:",["Individual marketing","Local marketing","Undifferentiated marketing","Differentiated marketing"],"Individual marketing is also called one-to-one marketing.","2026-10-21T19:12:00+05:00"],
 ["A",2,"A supermarket chain stocks more fishing gear in its Addu branch and more office snacks in its Malé branch. This is:",["Local marketing","Undifferentiated marketing","Concentrated marketing","Individual marketing"],"Local marketing tailors the offer to local customer groups.","2026-10-21T19:12:00+05:00"],
 ["A",2,"A luxury resort offers private butlers and underwater dining at very high prices. Which value proposition is this?",["More for more","More for less","The same for less","Less for much less"],"Top quality at a high price: more for more.","2026-10-21T19:12:00+05:00"],
 ["A",2,"A travel agency targets 'adventure seekers' who love diving, surfing and trying new things. Which segmentation base is this?",["Psychographic","Geographic","Demographic","Occasion"],"Lifestyle and personality are psychographic.","2026-10-21T19:12:00+05:00"],
 ["A",3,"A new supermarket in Hulhumalé sells the same well-known brands as its rivals, but at lower prices. Which value proposition is this?",["The same for less","More for more","More for the same","Less for much less"],"Same quality and brands at a lower price: the same for less.","2026-10-21T19:12:00+05:00"]
